  "question": {
    "text": "A vector <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math> has components <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>p</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math> with respect to a rectangular cartesian system. This system is rotated through a certain angle about the origin in the counter clockwise sense. If, with respect to new system, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math> has components <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>10</mn></msqrt><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;then a value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi></math> is equal to:"
